This program reads the voltage from the Honeywell MICROpeL MP-741 combustible gas sensor using an MCP3008 ADC connected via SPI to a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It continuously prints the voltage and a placeholder PPM value to the console every second and appends a timestamp, voltage, and PPM to a file named `gas_log.txt`. It handles SPI initialization and transfer errors, and gracefully closes resources on SIGINT (Ctrl+C). The program runs as a simulated propane leak detector until interrupted.

