This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It initializes GPIO pins 17 (TRIGGER), 18 (ECHO), and 27 (BUZZER) with the appropriate direction and configuration. It then sets up an interrupt handler for GPIO 18 to capture both the rising and falling edges of the echo signal from an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor.

