This program initializes the I2C and GPIO subsystems, sets up a circular buffer for pressure readings, and enters a loop where it samples the BMP180 sensor every 50 ms. It computes a rolling average of the pressure readings and compares each new reading to this average to detect deviations. If a deviation greater than 5 hPa is detected, it asserts an active-HIGH alert on GPIO24 and logs the alert to stderr. The program also handles I2C errors and sensor absence.

The `cleanup` function is included for completeness, but in this case, since the main loop already handles SIGINT by releasing resources and terminating the program, it remains empty.

