This code initializes the BMP180 sensor, reads its calibration data, and then samples temperature and pressure every 500 ms. It uses a hardware timer to trigger these samples and drives a cooling fan connected to GPIO18 when the temperature exceeds 30°C. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by turning off the fan and cleaning up resources. The BMP180 library `libgpiod` is used for I2C communication and GPIO control, ensuring compatibility with modern Raspberry Pi systems.

