This C program reads from four GPIO pins connected to Keywish KY-032 sensors and controls an LED based on the sensor readings. It uses the `gpiod` library for GPIO operations and handles errors during GPIO initialization. The program also sets up a signal handler to gracefully exit when it receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal. It polls the GPIO inputs every 50 milliseconds without using blocking delays, ensuring responsiveness to immediate sensor changes. Upon exit or receipt of a signal, it releases all GPIO resources to prevent resource leaks.

