This C program initializes SPI communication on Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using SPI bus 0 with CS0 on GPIO8, sets the maximum clock speed to 1 MHz, and configures the SPI mode to 3. It reads the gyroscope and accelerometer data from the Analog Devices ADIS16448 IMU using the single-register read protocol, applies the appropriate scaling factors, and logs the data to the console every 100 ms.

The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by ignoring them to prevent abrupt termination. On exit, it cleans up by closing the SPI device file and the SPI driver library to release resources.

Please ensure that the `GYRO_REG` and `ACCEL_REG` constants are defined with the correct register addresses for your specific IMU model. The scaling factors (`GYRO_SCALE` and `ACCEL_SCALE`) should also be adjusted according to the datasheet of your IMU.

Note: This code assumes that the SPI library (`libgpiod`) is available and correctly installed on your system. If `libgpiod` is not available, you may need to use `pigpio` or another library that supports SPI communication on Raspberry Pi. Adjustments to the SPI initialization and read operations would be necessary in that case.

