This C program creates a smart lighting sunrise effect on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using four SRD-05VDC relay modules connected to GPIO pins 17, 18, 27, and 22 (BCM numbering). It uses a 1 kHz hardware PWM signal to gradually increase the intensity of the relays over a 30-minute period, stepping the change every second. The program logs every event with timestamps to a file named `smart_lighting.log`, verifies GPIO pin mode setup, and handles PWM initialization failures gracefully. It also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including proper handling of SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

