This C program uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up a signal handler to clean up resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM, and continuously monitors the IR sensor and toggles the relay accordingly. Each state change is logged to a file named `relay_events.log` with an ISO 8601 timestamp. The program handles initialization failures, GPIO read/write errors, and log file write errors, ensuring robust operation and resource cleanup on exit.

