This C program uses the `gpiod` library to control GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi. It sets up GPIO18 as a PWM output for controlling a servo motor, and GPIO21 and GPIO22 as input pins with pull-up resistors for lock and unlock buttons respectively. The program debounces button presses with a 100 ms delay and adjusts the servo pulse width accordingly. It also handles SIGINT signals to ensure a clean exit and resource release.

