4. Sending an "EMERGENCY STOP!" message to the UART when all three sensors detect an obstacle.
5. Handling SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing the UART, releasing GPIO resources, and terminating the program.
6. Cleaning up resources on all exit paths, including closing the UART and releasing GPIO resources.

